  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">We Effect EU own contribution Zimbabwe 2019-2022</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">We Effect EU-egeninsats Zimbabwe 2019-2022</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Insatsens m&#xe5;l &#xe4;r att bidra till st&#xe4;rkt kapacitet hos det civila samh&#xe4;llet och &#xf6;kad medvetenhet, engagemang och kapacitet hos m&#xe4;nniskor som lever i fattigdom att arbeta f&#xf6;r demokrati och organisera sig f&#xf6;r att kunna utkr&#xe4;va sina m&#xe4;nskliga r&#xe4;ttigheter. Insatsen syftar &#xe4;ven till att &#xf6;ka samarbetet mellan civilsamh&#xe4;llesorganisationer, regeringen och den offentliga och privata sektorn inom Dairy Value Chain (DVC) genom att bidra med gemensamma plattformar f&#xf6;r dialog, f&#xf6;rhandling och finansiering.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">We Effect har ans&#xf6;kt om finansiering av egeninsats om 7 193 708 SEK f&#xf6;r EU-projektet &quot;Zimbabwe Agriculture Growth Programme: Transforming Zimbabwes Dairy Value Chain for the future&quot; under &#xe5;ren 2019-2022. 

Insatsen syftar till att:

&quot;Address the root causes of underperformance in the Dairy Value Chain (DVC) in Zimbabwe by strengthening the linkages between production, processing and financing. It seeks to improve DVC economic, social and environmental performance through inclusive business models, targeting and use of climate smart dairy farming and renewable energy, respectively. It further seeks to influence DVC policies, engage stakeholders and lobby for an enabling policy environment&quot;.

Insatsen har en total budget p&#xe5; 6 999 610 EUR, vilket motsvara cirka 73 996 377 SEK. S&#xf6;kt st&#xf6;d fr&#xe5;n Sida &#xe4;r 7 193 708 SEK, vilket motsvarar cirka 10 procent av den totala budgeten.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">We Effect has applied to Sida for funding of 7 193 708 SEK to carry out the EU-project &quot;Zimbabwe Agriculture Growth Programme: Transforming Zimbabwes Dairy Value Chain for the future&quot; during the period 2019-2022. 

The project aims to:

&quot;Address the root causes of underperformance in the Dairy Value Chain (DVC) in Zimbabwe by strengthening the linkages between production, processing and financing. It seeks to improve DVC economic, social and environmental performance through inclusive business models, targeting and use of climate smart dairy farming and renewable energy, respectively. It further seeks to influence DVC policies, engage stakeholders and lobby for an enabling policy environment&quot;.

The contribution&apos;s total budget is 6 999 610 EUR, corresponding to approximately 73 996 377 SEK. The requested support from Sida is 7 193 708 SEK, which corresponds to 10 per cent of the total budget.</narrative>
  </description>
